# Build output
/build/
/out/

# Visual Studio
/.vs/
*.vcxproj*
*.sln
*.user

# CMake
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
cmake_install.cmake

# IDE / editor
/.idea/
/.vscode/
compile_commands.json

# Compiled shaders (generated into build/)
*.spv

# Generated at runtime (ImGui window layout)
imgui.ini

# Ad-hoc debug logs. The GUI build produces no capturable stdout (see
# docs/DEV_ENVIRONMENT.md #2), so logging to a file is the documented way to get
# runtime diagnostics — which means stray *.log files are a normal by-product of
# debugging, not something to commit.
*.log

# Hot-reload: uniquely-named live copies of the game DLL the loader makes each
# reload (Phase 12C). Normally created in the build output dir, but ignore them
# anywhere in case the executable is run from elsewhere.
*_live_*.dll

# M4 game modules. A game (its Game.dll of behaviours, import lib, and export) lives
# OUTSIDE this repo by policy (E:\Sugar Engine - Games\...). These patterns are a guard
# for the case where a game is ever configured/built inside the tree: the build output is
# never source. (Game.pdb / Game_live_*.dll are already covered above.)
Game.dll
Game.exp
Game.lib

# Crash reports (CrashHandler writes ./crashes/crash_*.dmp + .txt at runtime)
/crashes/

# Debug symbols (MSVC). Emitted into /build/ already, but ignore stray copies too --
# never source, and the game DLL build (M4) drops a Game.pdb beside the DLL.
*.pdb

# SaveData runtime store (core/SaveData). A game points it at <gameDir>/save.dat; if the
# engine is ever run from the repo it would write ./save.dat. Runtime state, never committed.
# `.tmp` is the half-written file SaveData::save renames from (atomic write), and `.good` is
# the copy the save-torture pass keeps to mutate; both are runtime debris.
save.dat
save.dat.tmp
save.good

# Measurement and probe output. The dogfood harnesses each write their own file rather than
# stdout, because a GUI build has no capturable stdout (docs/DEV_ENVIRONMENT.md #2). Covered
# by *.log above; named here so it is obvious these are *results*, reproducible by re-running
# the harness, and never source:
#   stream_test.log  chunk-boundary lifetime counters   (SUGAR_VOXEL_STREAMTEST)
#   edit_stress.log  large-world persistence verify     (SUGAR_VOXEL_EDITSTRESS/EDITVERIFY)
#   phase_log.log    per-phase cost of a chunk crossing (SUGAR_VOXEL_PHASELOG)
#   nav_test.log     navigation vs a changing world     (SUGAR_VOXEL_NAVTEST)
#   swim_test.log    off-mesh link traversal            (SUGAR_VOXEL_SWIMTEST)
#   torture.log      adversarial stress pass            (SUGAR_VOXEL_TORTURE)
#   voxel_debug.log  the voxel game's own trace

# Standalone export output for an EXTERNAL game (M4). `SUGAR_PACKAGE=1 SUGAR_GAME=<dir>`
# writes <dir>/dist, which is outside this repo by policy — but a game configured inside the
# tree would put it here, and a package is build output either way.
dist/

# OS files
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# Development docs (docs/) stay out of the repo until the engine is complete.
# They are working records -- architecture decisions mid-flight, toolchain traps,
# per-phase lessons -- and they change with the code they describe. They ship when
# the platform does; the design record behind Runtime UI is the first one earmarked
# for publication (see ROADMAP.md, M3 completion).
#
# The top-level docs (README, ROADMAP, RULES, REQUIREMENTS_AND_SCOPE) stay tracked.
/DevDocs/

# Cooked asset artifacts (Phase 19B). Derived from source assets + .meta settings,
# reproducible byte-for-byte, and safe to delete wholesale -- so never committed.
# Covered by /build/ already; named here because the cache is an asset-pipeline
# concept, not a build-system one, and deleting /build/ should not look like the
# only reason it is ignored.
/build/assetcache/

# Standalone export output (Phase 20). A package is fully reproducible from source via
# SUGAR_PACKAGE=1 -- cooked artifacts + manifest + copied scenes -- so it is build
# output, never committed. Under /build/ already; named for the same reason the cache is.
/build/package/
